<title>CHINA: China '97 grain supply/demand/prices stable-agency.</title>
<headline>China '97 grain supply/demand/prices stable-agency.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's grain supply and demand situation and market prices will be stable throughout 1997, the Xinhua news agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>It said adequate supply was behind stable flour prices in most places in China, as total 1996 grain output was more than 480 million tonnes and stocks had increased.</p>
<p>It gave no details of stocks.</p>
<p>Supply of grain for feed and industrial use had increased rapidly in recent years as per capita grain consumption had fallen, it said.</p>
<p>Between 1990 and 1995, annual per capita grain consumption in China's urban areas had fallen to 97 kg from 130 kg, while rural consumption had fallen to 259 kg from 262 kg.</p>
<p>Another reason was that domestic and international grain prices had become more closely linked, with low world prices affecting falls in the domestic Chinese grain price.</p>
<p>China announced a total grain crop in 1996 of 490 million tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
